<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>4.8.1: Comparing Changes in Output Based on Input</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00981</md:content-id>
    <md:title>4.8.1: Comparing Changes in Output Based on Input</md:title>
    <md:uuid>7202ecaa-f05a-4ef1-94c6-8abcbe661cdc</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><title>Warm Up Activity</title>
<para>Here are the recorded temperatures at three different times on a winter evening.</para> 
<table class="os-raise-horizontaltable">
  <thead/>
  <tbody>
    <row>
      <entry><emphasis>
        time
      </emphasis></entry><entry>
        4 p.m.
      </entry>
      <entry>
        6 p.m.
      </entry>
      <entry>
        10 p.m.
      </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry><emphasis>
        temperature
      </emphasis></entry><entry>
        25°F
      </entry>
      <entry>
        17°F
      </entry>
      <entry>
        8°F
      </entry>
    </row>
  </tbody>
</table>

<list>
  <item>Tyler says the temperature dropped faster between 4 p.m. and 6 p.m.</item>
  <item>Mai says the temperature dropped faster between 6 p.m. and 10 p.m.</item>
</list>

<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>Who do you agree with? Be prepared to show your reasoning.</para>
  </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answers:</para>
    <list>
      <item>I agree with Mai. The temperature dropped 8°F between 4 p.m. and 6 p.m., but it fell 9°F between 6 p.m. and 10 p.m.</item>
      <item>I agree with Tyler. The temperature dropped 4°F per hour between 4 p.m. and 6 p.m. It fell less than 4°F per hour in the evening.</item>
    </list>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End --></section>
</content>
